# SPEC-Driven Development

## Entry rule

No free-text requirements. Work starts from `specs/*.yaml` (use `SPEC-TEMPLATE.yaml`).

## Required fields

```yaml
spec:
  id: SPEC-<SCOPE>-<NNN>
  version: v0.1.0
  status: ACTIVE          # CREATE/DEPRECATED not dispatchable
  type: feature           # feature|bugfix|refactor|docs|infra|...
  feature_goal: ""        # one sentence, testable
  affected_files: []      # planned paths; 1-9 total for SPEC
  validation_rules: []    # e.g. "npm test PASS"
  replay_cases: []        # ≥1 if business logic; [] only with replay_exempt note
```

## Lifecycle

`ACTIVE → (tasks) → IMPLEMENTING → TESTING → DONE`

Split into **≤3 tasks** per SPEC (`tasks/`). Each task ≤3 files.

## Task card link

Every implementation task must cite `spec_id` and live in `tasks/TASK-*.yaml`.
